[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "King's Gambit"]
[Variation "King's Gambit Declined: 3.fxe5 Qh4+"]
[ECO "C30"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "black"]
[Tricks "trap,fork,mate-threat"]
[Themes "e1-h4-diagonal,king-in-the-centre"]
[Refutes "1. e4 e5 2. f4 Bc5 3. fxe5"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "for-us"]
[Opponent "3.fxe5"]
[Start "1. e4 e5 2. f4 Bc5"]

3. fxe5 $2 { Takes a pawn but leaves the f-file and the king exposed, because nothing guards h4 and g3. } 3... Qh4+ { Check on the e1-h4 diagonal. White has no good block or king move. } 4. g3 ( 4. Ke2 Qxe4# ) 4... Qxe4+ { Check again. It also attacks the rook on h1 behind the e4 pawn. } 5. Qe2 Qxh1 { Wins the rook. White's king is stuck in the centre and Black is far ahead. } *
